Scientific direction review — retained local analysis failures
Date: 2026-10-21 local / 2026-10-20 UTC
These are analysis-script mistakes, not model, API, experiment, or source-data failures.

1. A2 aggregation attempt grouped only by trajectory_sha256_prefix. This collapsed 40 matched rows into 2 trajectory classes. The denominator check exposed the error; corrected key is (group_sha256_prefix, trajectory_sha256_prefix). No results were accepted from the incorrect aggregate.

2. First row-count aggregation attempt used an undefined variable name in a list-comprehension. Python raised NameError before any result was written.

3. Second row-count aggregation attempt used a different undefined variable name. Python raised NameError before any result was written.

4. Third row-count aggregation attempt passed a Boolean directly to sum() instead of an iterable. Python raised TypeError before any result was written.

5. First candidate-matrix generator draft contained an incorrect pinned hash for configs/m1-100-scenarios.json. It stopped with M1_100_SCENARIO_SOURCE_HASH_MISMATCH before writing a file. The hash was read from the tracked file and pinned correctly.

6. The corrected candidate generator wrote the deterministic JSON, then failed while formatting a relative output path supplied from PowerShell. The JSON itself passed --check; the path reporting was corrected and the generator was rerun to completion.

7. An initial cost statement must use the current official Flash off-peak cache-miss/output rates ($0.15/$0.60 per million), not the separate Pro-column prices or a historical price snapshot. The draft budget was recalculated at 216 requests × 10,000 input tokens + 512 output tokens = $0.3903552 worst-case off-peak, under a proposed $0.45 hard cap. No request was sent.

8. The first `researchctl audit` after appending the new candidate records failed because three newly inserted SHA-256 references were uppercase. All reference values were normalized to lowercase; the same audit then passed with no errors and no open experiments. The failure and repair changed metadata only.

9. The first deterministic `--check` path in the new synthesis script passed bytes to the Path-only digest helper and raised AttributeError. It was corrected to hash the byte string directly; the repeated `--check` then returned PASS with output SHA-256 92fab36d07b002d3fbdd7d9454cba113ea41ccd72938a0ba961cea24ed4c16df. No source row or model output was modified.

10. A saved `researchctl audit` initially failed after the official pricing snapshot was added to the draft, because the mutable memory/candidate draft hash references still pointed to the preceding draft version. The current draft hash was recomputed and all three mutable records were updated; the repeated audit passed. No registered protocol, authorization record, or closed result changed.

No failed attempt removed or replaced an assigned experiment row. No raw private message, request body, response body, or credential is included in this log.
